# lib

`src/lib/` owns shared data contracts, fetching, validation, and catalog configuration.

## Module naming rules

Scope: `src/lib/`. Use kebab-case TypeScript basenames, for example `site-settings.ts`, with adjacent `<basename>.test.ts` tests. Keep modules directly in this folder unless they form an existing feature subfolder. Preserve generated files and framework-required names.

Executable filename conventions for this folder; preserve dot suffixes for tests and declarations.

```structures-rules
{
  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "module-names",
      "match": "**/*.{ts,tsx,mts,cts}",
      "case": "kebab-case"
    }
  ]
}
```
